Purpose of changes (include the issue number and title text for each relevant GitHub issue):
- Izumi GNU builds failed on BOZ literals (e.g. src/control/cam_history.F90:
  gen_hash_key_offset = z'000053db'): the forked machines/izumi/gnu_izumi.cmake had
  dropped the upstream unconditional
  string(APPEND FFLAGS " -fallow-argument-mismatch -fallow-invalid-boz ").
- Izumi NAG builds of theta-l / theta-l_kokkos failed ("ERROR:  is not in PATH?"):
  CAM's buildlib builds Kokkos for both targets and nag.cmake defined no C++
  compiler.  Use GNU C++ (MPICXX mpicxx, SCXX g++) alongside NAG Fortran, as is
  already done for C.  (NAG theta-l then stops at E3SM's sort_mod.F90, #102.)
- #103: Izumi Intel (20.0.1) runs segfaulted in routines with large automatic
  arrays (e.g. RRTMG rrtmg_sw_spcvmc.f90 line 300; earlier seen in COMPOSE) because
  they were placed on the stack.  Add -heap-arrays 64 for Izumi Intel.

